== Section 1: the weights sum to less than 1 ==
unary:  q = sum of 6^-size over terms = 0.750000000 (closed form 3/4); all identity sets (even number of terms, then the end marker): (1/6)/(1-q^2) = 0.380952381 = 8/21
binary: q = 3 - sqrt(5) = 0.763932023;  all identity sets: (1/7)/(1-q^2) = 0.343070232
        check of the closed form: partial sum of T_s/7^s up to s = 400 is 0.763932023
        number of terms of size 1..8: [4, 4, 20, 52, 228, 804, 3444, 13780];  T_s/T_(s-1) at s = 100, 1000, 3000: 4.9256, 4.9925, 4.9975  (limit 5)
        sum of T_s/5^s up to s = 3000: 1.967432  (the generating function at its singularity 1/5 is exactly 2,
        since T = 4z + zT + zT^2 at z = 1/5 reads (T - 2)^2 = 0; hence the weight of the terms of size > m is at most 2 (5/7)^(m+1))

== Corollary 4: eps(m) = (1/a) (1/(1-q^2) - 1/(1-q_m^2)) ==
  n   log2[7^13 eps(n+1)] (addition)   36.5-0.485n   log2[6^5 eps(n)] (successor)   13-1.58n   log2 n
   10          26.85                     31.65              -2.95                  -2.80       3.3
   20          20.85                     26.80             -18.80                 -18.60       4.3
   50           4.56                     12.25             -66.35                 -66.00       5.6
  100         -21.11                    -12.00            -145.60                -145.00       6.6
  200         -71.11                    -60.50            -304.10                -303.00       7.6
  500        -218.68                   -206.00            -779.59                -777.00       9.0
 1000        -462.89                   -448.50           -1572.07               -1567.00      10.0
  the addition bound 7^13 eps(n+1) is below 1 first at n = 59 (so it says nothing for n < 59);
  the closed form 2^(36.5-0.485n) is below 1 first at n = 76
  the successor bound 6^5 eps(n) is below 1 first at n = 9
  7^13 eps(n+1) <= 2^(36.5-0.485n) for all n <= 3000: True  (largest log2 of the ratio: -2.9309, at n = 1)
  6^5 eps(n) <= 2^(13-1.58n) for all n <= 3000: True  (largest log2 of the ratio: -0.1408)
  for every n: eps(n+1) <= 1.2845 (5/7)^n, and (5/7)^n / 2^(-0.485 n) = 0.999704^n;
  so the stated inequality holds for all n >= 836 by this estimate, and for n <= 3000 by the exact computation: for all n.
  asymptotic slope: log2(7/5) = 0.48543 (stated 0.485); unary: log2 3 = 1.58496 (stated 1.58)

== Section 6.2: what the enumeration covers (unary f, sets of at most 12 symbols) ==
identities up to renaming and swapping, sizes 2..12: 51297  (eq_unary reports 51297)
ordered lists of concrete identities with at most 12 symbols: 91552735; their total weight: 0.352913217273  (eq_unary count mode: 0.352913217272)
weight of all identity sets of any size: 0.380952380952; so sets of more than 12 symbols weigh 0.028039 = 7.4% of the prior
identity sets of at most 12 symbols up to renaming, swapping and reordering (multisets): 476610
   (eq_unary count mode reports 476610; the 200,093 of the note is the number of search nodes it visits, namely the
    sets found consistent plus the inconsistent sets whose predecessor in its search order is consistent)
